provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":13,"output":398,"cacheRead":18706,"cacheWrite":605,"totalTokens":19722,"cost":{"input":0.000013,"output":0.00199,"cacheRead":0.0018706000000000003,"cacheWrite":0.00075625,"total":0.0046298500000000005},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":160},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786912029568,"responseId":"msg_011Ce74FbwcRmbXcQzEeNuMz","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01UzMsNs24UMGHuLHRc5D9LL","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"total\"\n7942\n\n(showing up to 50 rows; pass limit or aggregate to count — do not page)"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786912034921},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01TksE9UfwnL61u8C3XF8Srf","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"POPESTIMATE2025\"\n341784857\n\n(showing up to 50 rows; pass limit or aggregate to count — do not page)"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786912034921},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! I have:\n- Total farmers markets (excluding territories): 7,942\n- 2025 U.S. population: 341,784,857\n\nNow I need to calculate: (7,942 / 341,784,857) * 100,000 = 2.3237 (approximately)\n\nBut I should do this calculation within the catalog as a composed metric, not in my head. Let me create a build script that creates this metric by joining the two datasets.\n\nActually, wait. I can use `xorq catalog compose` to create this metric from the farmers_markets data since the population is a single row. But the instructions say not to use compose for cross-dataset metrics - I need to use a build script that reads both sources and joins them.\n\nLet me create a build script that:\n1. Reads the farmers markets data\n2. Reads the census population data\n3. Filters to exclude territories\n4. Filters census to just \"United States\"\n5. Calculates the metric","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll create a build script to compute the metric by joining both datasets:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_011EHSZ55k7JVmJCLMZRm1BY","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/farmers_markets_per_capita.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener(); _o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]; u.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\n# Read both sources\nmarkets = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con,\n    storage_options=so\n)\n\npopulation = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con,\n    storage_options=so\n)\n\n# Filter markets to exclude territories (keep 50 states + DC)\nmarkets_excl = (\n    markets.filter(markets.state_name != \"Puerto Rico\")\n    .filter(markets.state_name != \"Virgin Islands\")\n)\n\n# Get total markets\ntotal_markets = markets_excl.aggregate(total_fm=markets_excl.farmers_markets.sum()).mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n\n# Get US population for 2025\nus_pop = (\n    population.filter(population.NAME == \"United States\")\n    .select(\"POPESTIMATE2025\")\n    .mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n)\n\n# Join and calculate metric\nexpr = (\n    total_markets.join(us_pop, total_markets.k == us_pop.k)\n    .mutate(markets_per_100k=total_markets.total_fm / us_pop.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n    .select(\"total_fm\", \"POPESTIMATE2025\", \"markets_per_100k\")\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":833,"cacheRead":19311,"cacheWrite":527,"totalTokens":20685,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.004165,"cacheRead":0.0019311000000000003,"cacheWrite":0.00065875,"total":0.00676885},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":231},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786912034921,"responseId":"msg_011Ce74F